;; Companion to kotoba-native kernel-object-entries `aiueos-browser-key`
;; (guest browser desktop input method, ADR-0225; the dictionary, ADR-0235).
;;
;; THE EXPECTED VALUES ARE THE ORACLE'S. Every key-sequence vector below was
;; produced by feeding its `:keys` to src/aiueos/compositor/ime.cljk
;; (`boot`, then `handle-key` per key) and reading back `:committed` (or
;; `:guest-log` with the IME off), `:buf`, `:preedit`, `:converting?`,
;; `:cand-idx` and `:reading`. Each step's :expected is how many code points
;; that key committed. The last step asserts the focused body (window 2,
;; seeded with 日本), the romaji length and bytes, and the conversion words.
;; The refusal vectors (-1 -2 -3 -5 -6 -8, release, repeat) are this object's
;; own bounds, which the oracle does not have.
;;
;; v2 (ADR-0235): the object takes the dictionary. Every vector runs against
;; os/aiueos/ime/aiueos-kanji.dic -- the file the kernel boots with and the
;; oracle reads -- placed in the image after the surface; the conversions'
;; expected candidates are the oracle's over that file (か 下 仮, ひ 卑,
;; かき 柿, やま 山 岾, しょう 傷 償 勝, くわわる 加). While a reading is
;; converted, word 444 is its record's word offset in that file (か 10779,
;; くわわる 16458), read off the file by an index walk written apart from the
;; object. The steps keep [key-code value]; the runner hands the object
;; key-code * 4 + value. `kaki|Space` used to name a reading the three-entry
;; dictionary lacked; かき is in this one (柿), so that vector types
;; `nihon|Space`.
;;
;; Keys are Linux evdev codes: letters US layout, 57 Space, 28 Enter,
;; 14 Backspace, 1 Escape, 2 is "1" (ignored).
;; 41 is the Hankaku/Zenkaku toggle (ADR-0228); its vectors' oracle is
;; src/aiueos/compositor/desktop.cljk `set-ime` with the flipped state (the
;; hosted handle-key has no toggle key), and they also assert word 432.
;; The six vectors marked ADR-0232 do NOT take the hosted IME as oracle: with
;; nothing composed it consumes Backspace and does nothing, where
;; browser.input maps Backspace to :text/edit :delete-backward. Their bodies
;; are browser.text-edit delete-backward with the caret at the end of the body
;; (where insert-text leaves it): the last code point goes, an empty body
;; stays empty. A conversion, a romaji byte or a preedit code point is still
;; taken first, as the hosted IME takes it.
;; The sixteen vectors marked ADR-0237 have no oracle either: Alt (evdev 56)
;; is held in word 431 from its press to its release, and a Tab (15) press
;; while it is held answers 256 + the id at the bottom of the stack (word 5)
;; and changes nothing else -- the :window/focus that browser-reduce applies
;; (browser-reduce-v1 kind 5). Written from the rule, apart from the object;
;; they assert the state words, window 2's body and word 431.
;; The twenty-three vectors marked ADR-0240 take browser.text-edit as oracle:
;; Shift (42, 54) is held in word 2035; Shift+Left / Shift+Right (105 / 106) are
;; move-caret -1 / +1 {:extend? true} on the focused body, whose selection is
;; kept as words 2036 (the window id) and 2037 (how many code points before the
;; body's end are selected); Backspace is delete-backward and a letter replaces
;; the selection (insert-text). They are printed by browser-selection-oracle.cljk.
;; The twenty-six vectors marked ADR-0241 are the clipboard: Ctrl (29, 97) is
;; held in word 2038; with it held C (46) over a selection answers 512 and V (47)
;; answers 513 -- :clipboard/write / :clipboard/read requests that change
;; nothing -- and, only when browser.desktop-backend `request` with the vector's
;; broker decision produces an effect, the completion follows: the same code
;; with value 3 and the clipboard (a length word, 64 code points; 260 bytes) in
;; place of the dictionary. A write completion copies the selection's text; a
;; read completion is browser.text-edit insert-text of the clipboard's text. -7
;; is a completion's clipboard refused (null, not 260 bytes, length past 64).
;; They are printed by browser-clipboard-oracle.cljk.
{:format :aiueos.browser-ime/v2
 :entry aiueos-browser-key
 :graph {:root aiueos.browser-ime
         :modules [aiueos.browser-ime]}
 :native {:target :x86_64-aiueos-kernel-v1
          :export "kotoba_aiueos_browser_key"
          :imports []
          :required-operations [kernel-load-u32 kernel-store-u32 kernel-subregion]}
 :arguments [:surface :surface-bytes :dictionary :dictionary-bytes :key-code*4+value]
 :oracle "src/aiueos/compositor/ime.cljk handle-key"
 :result {:kind :committed-count-or-reason :range [-8 -1]
          :window-focus "256 + window id: Alt+Tab, a :window/focus for browser-reduce (ADR-0237)"
          :clipboard-request "512 Ctrl+C (:clipboard/write), 513 Ctrl+V (:clipboard/read): a request for the permission broker (ADR-0241)"}
 :reasons {-1 :null-region-or-surface-not-8192
           -2 :abi-or-window-count-outside-1-4
           -3 :focus-is-not-a-window-1-4
           -5 :the-body-would-pass-64
           -6 :dictionary-not-aiueos-dict-v1-or-record-out-of-bounds
           -7 :completion-clipboard-null-not-260-bytes-or-length-past-64
           -8 :romaji-buffer-full-or-preedit-overflow}
 :verification {:node-stack-size 8000
                :fuel 1048576
                :memory {:base 4096 :image-bytes 8192
                         :dictionary-file "os/aiueos/ime/aiueos-kanji.dic"
                         :dictionary-sha256 "b1b1664c48aa79fdaf45649a0faa9aaac8185278bffd50fdc4261443873efa6b"
                         :dictionary-bytes 189892}
                :floors {:minimum-vectors 120
